	<groupings>

		<!-- THE SUBMENU-PRESERVING GROUP. Do not rename these shortcuts.

		     Every `name` below is deliberately identical to a <submenu name="">
		     template above, and that identity is the ONLY thing in Skin
		     Shortcuts 3.0.1 that stops the shortcut picker from deleting a main
		     menu item's submenu.

		     pickers.py:200-208 is the whole mechanism:

		         if shortcut.name:
		             template = config.get_default_menu(shortcut.name)
		             if template and template.is_submenu:
		                 new_submenu = shortcut.name
		         if new_submenu != previous_submenu:
		             set_submenu(...); drop_per_item_submenu(...)

		     get_default_menu (config.py:242) searches default_menus, which is
		     every <menu> AND <submenu> parsed out of this file. So a picked
		     shortcut named "movies" resolves to the <submenu name="movies">
		     seventeen-item template, new_submenu becomes "movies", it equals the
		     item's own submenu="movies", and the destructive branch is never
		     entered. Rename the shortcut and get_default_menu returns None,
		     new_submenu is None, and manager.py:143-151 runs
		     `del self.working["mainmenu/movies"]` on the way past.

		     Measured before this group existed: 8 of the 12 main menu items
		     carry a submenu, the picker could reach 18 leaves, and 144 of 144
		     item/leaf combinations wiped the submenu. Zero preserved it, because
		     the only static leaves were browse-mode ones and pickers.py:707-719
		     replaces a browse-mode pick with a fresh Shortcut named
		     browse-{hash}. A browse-mode or <content> leaf can therefore NEVER
		     preserve a submenu; only an action-mode shortcut named after a
		     template can, which is what these twelve are.

		     One action each, on purpose. <action> inside a groupings shortcut
		     has no condition attribute (loaders/menu.py:696-702 reads text
		     only), so copying an item's two or three conditional actions here
		     would emit them as unconditional siblings and Kodi would run all of
		     them on one click. Each entry therefore carries the item's primary
		     action alone.

		     games, pictures, favorites and weather have no submenu template by
		     design (see control 405's gate in script-skinshortcuts.xml), so for
		     those four new_submenu is None either way and there is nothing to
		     preserve. They are here so the list is the whole home menu. -->
		<group name="sections" label="$LOCALIZE[31200]" icon="DefaultFolder.png">
