		     rows behind this group are: content.py's _resolve_commands returns
		     Quit, Reboot, Power off, Suspend, Hibernate, Restart and Reload
		     skin, and this skin already files all seven under extras/icons/Power
		     menu/. The label was $LOCALIZE[13012] "Exit" until 2026-07-31, which
		     is the label of ONE of the seven, so the picker drew a group called
		     "Exit >" whose first child was also called "Exit". -->
		<group name="commands" label="$LOCALIZE[31072]" icon="DefaultProgram.png">
			<content source="commands"/>
		</group>

		<!-- Raw action entry is the "Custom action..." row the add-on pins to the
		     TOP of the "Change action" picker (pickers.py _prompt_custom_action),
		     with a clear label and the item's current action pre-filled. A second
		     <input for="action"> used to sit here as the LAST grouping, but
		     $LOCALIZE[1024] is empty in Kodi 22, so it rendered as a blank,
		     unlabelled row that no one could recognise as "type an action" - the
		     exact reason the picker read as unable to reach an arbitrary window.
		     Removed 2026-08-03; do not re-add it. The keyboard path is the top row
		     now, not a mystery row at the bottom. -->

	</groupings>

</menus>
